    "northStar": "Campus wayfinding",
    "overview": "The native JavaFX workspace uses a navy course rail, a quiet cool ground and aligned task rows to make course, deadline and state easy to scan. Blue identifies actions and selection; timing and completion receive restrained semantic color and explicit words.\n\nThis is a code-led record of the implemented desktop surface, with no approved visual comp. Evidence is `src/main/resources/studytask.css`, `src/main/java/studytask/view/TaskView.java`, `PRODUCT.md`, `.impeccable/surfaces/workspace.md` and the desktop, compact, empty and error captures in `.impeccable/review/`. The existing course architecture follows these visual sections unchanged.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Native controls with visible keyboard focus.",
      "Aligned task rows with course and relative deadline context.",
      "Flat surfaces separated by tone and fine borders.",
      "Adjacent editing with persistent actions and retained input on errors."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Words With State Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "Pair semantic color with explicit status, priority or relative deadline text."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Persistent Actions Rule",
        "section": "layout",
        "body": "Scroll the editor fields independently while keeping feedback and save, status, clear and delete actions in the editor's bottom region."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "section": "elevation",
        "body": "Use tone and borders to separate the workspace regions."
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do pair semantic color with explicit status, priority or relative deadline text.",
      "Do keep the task list visible while editing and preserve input on errors.",
      "Do keep action feedback and editor actions outside the scrollable fields.",
      "Do use native controls with visible focus and associated field labels."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't treat the provisional direction sizes as shipped typography values.",
      "Don't introduce decorative shadows or motion into the flat workspace without an approved system change.",
